     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu ate 1/3 of a cake and Meena ate 1/4.\n\"How much did they eat?\" asked Mother."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "common denominator",
     "lowest form",
     "improper fraction"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To add or subtract fractions with different denominators, find a common denominator. The least common multiple of 3 and 4 is 12, so 1/3 is 4/12 and 1/4 is 3/12.\nThen add or subtract the numerators: 4/12 plus 3/12 is 7/12.\nMixed numbers can be changed to improper fractions before adding. Always write the answer in lowest form."
    }
   },
